From 7ba63b85effa020199be413921ed4ffc68e23e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Root <me@rooty.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:28:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] crosvm: --prefault-memory, guest RAM faulted in and on
 2 MiB pages

A guest under crosvm stalled for a frame of 20-40 ms at a time, in bursts,
where the same guest under nesbox did not: SuperTuxKart's 0.1% low at 4K
was 35-37 fps against nesbox's 72-82. Guest RAM is a memfd, and crosvm
leaves every page of it to the guest's first touch: a second-level fault
and a host page fault that allocates and zeroes one 4 KiB page, each time a
guest program reaches memory the guest has not used yet -- which a game
does in bursts long after boot. Touching the guest's free memory from
inside the guest first took the lows to nesbox's. And a memfd's huge pages
are the host's shmem policy's, upstream's default `never` giving none, so
every guest access also walked 4 KiB second-level pages.

--prefault-memory starts a thread as the vCPUs start that
MADV_POPULATE_WRITEs all of guest RAM (a page the guest reached first is
left as it is; nothing is written), then MADV_COLLAPSEs it into 2 MiB pages
one block at a time -- which a `never` host allows, and which over a whole
range would stop at the first block it cannot allocate. It runs only once
every device process is forked (minijail refuses to fork a process with a
thread of its own), and not for a VM whose memory the host may not touch.
An 8 GiB guest was faulted in after 1.0 s and all on 2 MiB pages after 2.5
s, and the 0.1% low above went to 80. The cost is the whole of guest RAM
committed as the VM starts.

A 2 MiB page of the file can back guest RAM only where the host address is
as far past a 2 MiB boundary as the file offset is. base's `align` for a
file mapping now means exactly that (the address aligned relative to the
offset; plain alignment for an aligned offset, as before), and with the
option guest RAM regions of 2 MiB or more are mapped so: the region at
1 MiB of guest memory is at offset 1 MiB of the file, and refused every
collapse otherwise.

